# OS / editor
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
# Python
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# Node
node_modules/
# Auto-generated at app startup (user/runtime-specific) — would go stale
**/references/mcp-catalog.md
**/references/skills-catalog.md
# Runtime scratch/output
scratch/
outputs/

# Working notes: design/plan documents kept beside the skills but not part of
# what is published. Nothing in the collection reads them -- they reference
# only each other.
docs/

# Secrets. A skill's .env holds real API keys (SerpAPI et al). Three of them
# were committed in the initial import and sat in a PUBLIC repo for months --
# the files even carried the comment "Gitignored — never commit this file",
# which was not true because no rule existed. It does now. Commit the
# .env.example beside it instead, as SEO/serp-shape already does.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example

# Editor leftovers. workflow-compile/SKILL.md.bak turned up alongside a real
# edit; a stale copy of a skill's instructions is worse than none, since the
# runtime reads SKILL.md by name and a reader cannot tell which is current.
*.bak
*.orig
*~
